# File Format Handling

## Supported Formats

| Format | Extensions | Description |
|--------|------------|-------------|
| EIGENSTRAT | .geno, .snp, .ind | Text-based genotype format |
| PackedAncestryMap | .geno (packed), .snp, .ind | Binary-packed EIGENSTRAT |
| PLINK | .bed, .bim, .fam | Binary genotype format |
| VCF | .vcf, .vcf.gz | Variant Call Format |

## File Prefix Convention

All formats use a common prefix pattern:
- EIGENSTRAT: `prefix.geno`, `prefix.snp`, `prefix.ind`
- PLINK: `prefix.bed`, `prefix.bim`, `prefix.fam`

```rust
// Detect format automatically
let format = detect_format(prefix)?;
let genotypes = match format {
    Format::Eigenstrat => read_eigenstrat(prefix)?,
    Format::Plink => read_plink(prefix)?,
    // ...
};
```

## Memory Mapping

Use `memmap2` for large files:

```rust
use memmap2::Mmap;

let file = File::open(path)?;
let mmap = unsafe { Mmap::map(&file)? };
```

## Streaming Reads

For very large datasets, use streaming API:

```rust
let reader = StreamingGenotypes::new(prefix)?;
for chunk in reader.chunks(10000) {
    process_chunk(chunk?);
}
```

## Test Data

Real datasets for integration tests:
- **AADR v66.p1**: `/references/aadr/v66.p1/v66.p1_1240K.aadr.patch.PUB.*` (TGENO); the goldens
  use `tests/golden/aadr/build_aadr_v66p1.py`'s labelled subset. Never v62.0 or v66.0.
- **AADR HO**: `/references/aadr_v54.1.p1/HO_public.*`
- **1000G**: `/8tb/1000genomes/`

## I/O Error Handling

Always provide file context in errors:

```rust
PopmixError::io_with_path(io_error, path)
PopmixError::parse(file, line, details)
```
